page 50 (
    name: Guide & safety boundary
    alias: GUIDE
    title: Guide & safety boundary | APEX Theme Manager
    appearance {
        pageTemplate: @/standard
        templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    }
    navigation {
        warnOnUnsavedChanges: false
    }
    security {
        authentication: required
        pageAccessProtection: argumentsMustHaveChecksum
    }


    region guide (
        name: A deliberate recovery workflow
        type: staticContent
        layout {
            sequence: 10
            slot: body
            columnSpan: 12
            startNewRow: true
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/hero
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
            icon: fa-clone
        }
        source {
            htmlCode: ```html
    <p class="apxtm-eyebrow">A COMMUNITY TOOL FOR DEVELOPMENT WORKSPACES</p><p class="apxtm-lead">Definitions are immutable evidence. A preview is an exact proposal. A verified operation is an independently checked result.</p>
    ```
        }
    
    
    )

    region workflow (
        name: From baseline to verified result
        type: staticContent
        layout {
            sequence: 20
            slot: body
            columnSpan: 12
            startNewRow: true
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/standard
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    
        }
        source {
            htmlCode: ```html
    <ol><li><strong>Register.</strong> Your database owner explicitly registers a development application and grants named actors access.</li><li><strong>Capture.</strong> Save a definition baseline before changing a layout.</li><li><strong>Compare.</strong> Capture the current definition and inspect classifications and eligibility.</li><li><strong>Select.</strong> Choose eligible properties or preview all eligible differences.</li><li><strong>Preview.</strong> Check the target, selected values, expiry and exact confirmation phrase.</li><li><strong>Apply.</strong> Submit the phrase. The engine reauthorizes, checks freshness, backs up, imports and verifies.</li></ol>
    ```
        }
    
    
    )

    region boundary (
        name: What can be recovered
        type: staticContent
        layout {
            sequence: 30
            slot: body
            columnSpan: 12
            startNewRow: true
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/standard
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    
        }
        source {
            htmlCode: ```html
    <p>The initial automatic scope covers recognized grid spans, positions and row or field booleans that are explicitly present in both exports. Matching requires stable application and component identity.</p><p>Template changes, cross-theme mappings, unknown expressions, absent properties and ambiguous matches are detection only. Review their reasons and use App Builder for deliberate edits.</p>
    ```
        }
    
    
    )

    region states (
        name: Read the report correctly
        type: staticContent
        layout {
            sequence: 40
            slot: body
            columnSpan: 12
            startNewRow: true
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/standard
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    
        }
        source {
            htmlCode: ```html
    <p><strong>Classification</strong> describes the observed change: unchanged, changed, added, dropped, no match, ambiguous, unsupported or conflict.</p><p><strong>Eligibility</strong> says whether an independently validated rule allows automatic recovery. <strong>Outcome</strong> records whether a selected property was fixed or failed.</p><p>A successful import return alone is not success. Only an operation marked <strong>VERIFIED</strong> passed the independent export check.</p>
    ```
        }
    
    
    )

    region recovery-policy (
        name: Access, backups and restores
        type: staticContent
        layout {
            sequence: 50
            slot: body
            columnSpan: 12
            startNewRow: true
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/standard
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    
        }
        source {
            htmlCode: ```html
    <p>The default modification policy is disabled. The manager itself is excluded. READ, RECOVER and RESTORE rights are checked by the server for the authenticated account.</p><p>Snapshot ZIP downloads contain application definitions and may include embedded application code. Keep them within your authorized workspace and access policy.</p><p>Definition restore is a separate preview with RESTORE authority and a separate typed confirmation. The snapshot and current application must have identical ACL assignment state; a difference is rejected for explicit manual review. The tool does not reset ACL assignments or restore database table data.</p><p>Import can commit or fail partially; inspect the operation and its backup after any failure.</p>
    ```
        }
    
    
    )

    region about (
        name: Original, source available and honest about scope
        type: staticContent
        layout {
            sequence: 60
            slot: body
            columnSpan: 12
            startNewRow: true
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/standard
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    
        }
        source {
            htmlCode: ```html
    <p>APEX Theme Manager is an independent B2DEV TECH community project. It uses native Oracle APEX Universal Theme components and public Oracle APIs. Oracle-generated exports warn that editing their SQL is unsupported. These APIs do not make transformed exports an Oracle-supported authoring contract; this beta is not Oracle-certified. The bundled Layout Lab is original synthetic content.</p><p>This beta has been exercised locally on APEX 26.2. Treat other releases as unverified until their parser, installation and browser gates have been run.</p>
    ```
        }
    
    
    )
)
